      "scope": "project",
      "source_uri": "docatlas://source/v2/f2926f30931f9aa001aa06bb"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev-c29435611bde8860a74f502d",
      "path_or_url": "cave-radio.md",
      "section": "Cave team equipment guide > Underground radio check",
      "snippet": "## Underground radio check\n\nThis procedure applies to the low-frequency radios used by the survey team below ground. Surface vehicle radios use a different check sheet.\n\n",
      "version_binding": "unversioned",
      "content_sha256": "b226e0703b552a153bdc3d916477c5e6e53c38604e205876012d18ea3b1b90e8",
      "project_identity": "local:505e3f3fa9f43844161d99171f979a802340ab7efbe44322b924bf217c225ec5",
      "line_start": 5,
      "line_end": 8,
      "authority": "source_of_truth",
      "scope": "project",
      "source_uri": "docatlas://source/v2/8a12fdeaa802113ffe1e83bf"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev-4fc8f5d2aa31c6310a356c45",
      "path_or_url": "cave-radio.md",
      "section": "Cave team equipment guide > Underground radio check > Antenna connection",
      "snippet": "### Antenna connection\n\nConnect the loop antenna to the marked socket before enabling the transmitter. Lay the loop flat and keep its cable clear of the footpath.\n\n",
      "version_binding": "unversioned",
      "content_sha256": "00ec0519645164d57c85f11e7cbe68f824d9dfe30e10d7b94486e4c2c06abc76",
      "project_identity": "local:505e3f3fa9f43844161d99171f979a802340ab7efbe44322b924bf217c225ec5",
      "line_start": 9,
      "line_end": 12,
      "authority": "source_of_truth",
      "scope": "project",
      "source_uri": "docatlas://source/v2/ae775d4d92fb807bc3eda8b4"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev-e5ff1541e00ffcb48aaa29fd",
      "path_or_url": "cave-radio.md",
      "section": "Cave team equipment guide > Underground radio check > Voice exchange",
      "snippet": "### Voice exchange\n\nAsk the surface operator to repeat the test phrase exactly and record the reply in the trip log. A carrier indication alone does not count as a completed radio check.\n\n",
      "version_binding": "unversioned",
      "content_sha256": "878698da89a19df7b0232651b8f7e8a4d19f56c8b7b39aba17abd8165e4cd675",
      "project_identity": "local:505e3f3fa9f43844161d99171f979a802340ab7efbe44322b924bf217c225ec5",
      "line_start": 13,
      "line_end": 16,
      "authority": "source_of_truth",
      "scope": "project",
      "source_uri": "docatlas://source/v2/898ac2bff3438462b2065c53"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev-ced8db941caeceec1aab3fd5",
      "path_or_url": "cave-radio.md",
      "section": "Cave team equipment guide > Underground radio check > Standby",
      "snippet": "### Standby\n\nAfter a successful voice exchange, place the transmitter in receive-only standby until the scheduled check-in. Leave the antenna connected during standby.\n\n",
      "version_binding": "unversioned",
      "content_sha256": "6eca893c45c1cdcfb20ce51c79c98571e7349406f74173085d32c9084e680f08",
      "project_identity": "local:505e3f3fa9f43844161d99171f979a802340ab7efbe44322b924bf217c225ec5",
      "line_start": 17,
      "line_end": 20,
      "authority": "source_of_truth",
      "scope": "project",
      "source_uri": "docatlas://source/v2/390a248a953d80085cfb945e"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev-174ecb097b7deb6418ff5772",
      "path_or_url": "cave-radio.md",
      "section": "Cave team equipment guide > Underground radio check > Storage labels",
      "snippet": "### Storage labels\n\nThe radio cases have orange inventory labels. Replacement labels are available in the stationery tray; their colour does not indicate battery charge or signal quality.\n\n",
      "version_binding": "unversioned",
      "content_sha256": "81ae322459d885983fa98b10da9a51ade5e1fc78b82cf29999b225f87682db94",
      "project_identity": "local:505e3f3fa9f43844161d99171f979a802340ab7efbe44322b924bf217c225ec5",
      "line_start": 21,
      "line_end": 24,
      "authority": "source_of_truth",
      "scope": "project",
      "source_uri": "docatlas://source/v2/4b5ec25cae6562afd3661012"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev-4914af9c8630c5542a96706d",
      "path_or_url": "cave-radio.md",
      "section": "Cave team equipment guide > Flood watch exception",
      "snippet": "## Flood watch exception\n\nDuring an active flood watch, the underground radio check does not authorize entering the cave even if the test phrase is repeated correctly. The expedition leader must formally clear the flood watch before entry.\n\n",
      "version_binding": "unversioned",
      "content_sha256": "12bb7a4dd59541e522cee1dc5ad094ee8bdfd04ca151134594192ac731ba999a",
      "project_identity": "local:505e3f3fa9f43844161d99171f979a802340ab7efbe44322b924bf217c225ec5",
      "line_start": 25,
      "line_end": 28,
      "authority": "source_of_truth",
      "scope": "project",
      "source_uri": "docatlas://source/v2/ca393346072a0cf6e2b75a84"
    }
